IMPORT prelude

-- Privacy Act 1988 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what may be done with my information, and what I must be told.
--
-- SEAT: the individual whose personal information is held (the borrower, the debtor, the customer, the user whose data is
-- breached, the employee) -- "Is the business that holds my information bound by the Act? Can I see it and correct it? Can I
-- stop the marketing? What may my credit file hold, and for how long? Must I be told of a breach? Will the Commissioner take
-- my complaint?". Every exported question is that person's. Where the Act hands a judgment to someone else (the entity being
-- satisfied or reasonably believing something; "a reasonable person would conclude"; the Commissioner considering a course
-- appropriate), it is asked as a fact, and the answer is conditional on it.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 6(1) "APP entity" (an agency or organisation); s 6C(1) (organisation, the small business operator
-- limb); s 6D(1)-(4), (7)-(9) (small business, small business operator, the $3,000,000 turnover test); s 6DA(1) (annual
-- turnover, as a fact); s 6DA(2) (the part-year formula); s 6EA(1) (the opt-in); s 7B(3) (employee records); Schedule 1, APP 7 (direct marketing), APP 12
-- (access), APP 13 (correction); Part IIIA: ss 6N, 6Q, 20K (ban period), 20R (access to my credit report), 20T (correction of
-- my credit file), 20V(2), 20W, 20X(1) items 4 and 5, 21C(1) (being told which credit reporting body), 21D(2), (3)(a), (b),
-- (d), 21P (notice that my credit was refused because of my credit report); Part IIIC: ss 26WE, 26WF(1), (2), 26WG (as a
-- fact), 26WH, 26WK, 26WL; Part V: ss 36(1), (3), (5), 40(1), (1A), (1B), 41(1)(c).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 104, compilation date 4 June 2026, includes amendments to Act No. 75, 2025 (register id
-- C2026C00227), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03712.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026), with the
-- s 6DA(2) formula from ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03712.formulas.md (transcribed by hand on 21 October 2026 from
-- the Word rendering of the same compilation).
-- NOT DEPOSITED: the Privacy Regulation 2013 (any higher default amount under s 6Q(1)(d)(ii), the matters prescribed for an
-- APP 12.9 or 13.3 notice, small business operators prescribed under s 6E) and the Privacy (Credit Reporting) Code 2014 (the
-- manner of access under s 20R(4), the extra matters in a s 21C or s 21P notice). The prescribed default amount is an INPUT;
-- the rest is not encoded.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: agencies' own regime beyond APP 12 and 13 deadlines and charges (FOI-based refusals are a fact); State
-- authorities and registered political parties; s 6E; ss 6D(5), (6) (private and non-business affairs; the trading flag
-- is taken as already narrowed by them and by (7), (8)); s 7B(1), (2), (4) and the other exemptions; APPs 1-6, 8-11; the APP 12.3 grounds one by
-- one (one fact: "an APP 12.3 ground applies"); the rest of Part IIIA (use and disclosure by credit reporting bodies, ss 20E-
-- 20N except 20K; repayment history conditions in s 21D(3)(c); credit providers' use of credit eligibility information,
-- ss 21G-21N; access to and correction of a credit provider's records, ss 21T-21V, except as a ground in s 40(1B); 20Y; the
-- CR code); bankruptcies and personal insolvency agreements in s 20X; the Part IIIC exceptions in ss 26WD, 26WJ, 26WM-26WQ
-- and the Commissioner's directions (s 26WR); representative complaints (ss 38-39); the rest of s 41, conciliation (s 40A),
-- determinations (s 52) and penalties; the statutory tort for serious invasions of privacy (Schedule 2). What a lender must
-- assess before a credit card is issued (c043, k048) is the National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009. Debt collectors'
-- conduct (k064) is not this Act. The National Personal Insolvency Index (k075) is the Bankruptcy Act 1966.
--
-- DATES are numbers YYYYMMDD (31 May 2042 is 20420531). "The period of N years that starts on" day D is over from D + N x
-- 10000 (its anniversary) onwards; "21 days after" is computed by the caller. This is the encoder's convention, not the Act's.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Privacy Act 1988 -- from the seat of the individual whose information is held`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- The day on which a period of N whole years starting on day D is over (the anniversary), in YYYYMMDD.
GIVEN `the start` IS A NUMBER, `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the anniversary` MEANS `the start` PLUS 10000 TIMES `years`

§§ `ss 6, 6C, 6D, 6DA, 6EA, 7B(3) -- is the holder of my information bound`

-- s 6(1): "APP entity means an agency or organisation."
-- s 6C(1): "organisation means: (a) an individual; or (b) a body corporate; or (c) a partnership; or (d) any other
-- unincorporated association; or (e) a trust; that is not a small business operator, a registered political party, an agency,
-- a State or Territory authority or a prescribed instrumentality of a State or Territory."
-- s 6D(1): "A business is a small business at a time (the test time) in a financial year (the current year) if its annual
-- turnover for the previous financial year is $3,000,000 or less." (2): "if there was no time in the previous financial year
-- when the business was carried on, the business is a small business at the test time only if its annual turnover for the
-- current year is $3,000,000 or less."
-- s 6DA(1): annual turnover is the total "earned in the year in the course of the business" (sales, commission, repair and
-- service income, rent, leasing and hiring, government bounties and subsidies, interest, royalties and dividends, other
-- operating income) -- the holder's figure, asked as a fact. (2): for part of a year, "the amount worked out using the
-- formula:" -- the formula is missing from the deposit; a part-year figure is an INPUT.
-- s 6D(3): a small business operator "(a) carries on one or more small businesses; and (b) does not carry on a business that is
-- not a small business". (4): it is NOT one if it "(a) carries on a business that has had an annual turnover of more than
-- $3,000,000 for a financial year that has ended after the later of" starting the business and commencement; "(b) provides a
-- health service to another individual and holds any health information except in an employee record; or (c) discloses
-- personal information about another individual to anyone else for a benefit, service or advantage; or (d) provides a benefit,
-- service or advantage to collect personal information"; "(e) is a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth contract";
-- "(f) is a credit reporting body". (7), (8): consent or legal authority takes (c) and (d) away. (9): a body corporate "related
-- to a body corporate that carries on a business that is not a small business" is not a small business operator.
-- s 6EA(1): the Act applies to a small business operator "as if the operator were an organisation while a choice by the
-- operator to be treated as an organisation is registered".
-- Simplification: one business per holder (s 6D(3)(b) is then the s 6D(1) test of that business).
DECLARE Holder HAS
    `is an agency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carried on the business at some time in the previous financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `annual turnover for the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER
    `annual turnover for the current year` IS A NUMBER
    `highest annual turnover for any financial year ended since it started` IS A NUMBER
    `provides a health service and holds health information outside employee records` IS A BOOLEAN
    `trades in personal information without consent or legal authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a credit reporting body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is related to a body corporate whose business is not small` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has registered a choice to be treated as an organisation` IS A BOOLEAN

`the small business turnover limit` MEANS 3000000

-- s 6DA(2): "if a business has been carried on for only part of a financial year, its annual turnover for the financial
-- year is the amount worked out using the formula:" The formula is an image the text deposit lost; it is transcribed in
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03712.formulas.md from the Word rendering of the same compilation:
--     Amount that would be the annual turnover of the business under subsection (1) if the part were a whole financial year
--       x (Number of days in the whole financial year / Number of days in the part)
-- The first term is read as the s 6DA(1) total earned in the part (the part treated as if it were the whole year).
@export What is the annual turnover of a business carried on for only part of a financial year (s 6DA(2))?
GIVEN `turnover earned in the part` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 6DA(1) total the business earned in the part of the year it was carried on, in dollars
      `days in the part` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the part of the financial year the business was carried on
      `days in the whole financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the whole financial year (365 or 366)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the annual turnover for a part year` IS
    IF `days in the part` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `turnover earned in the part` TIMES `days in the whole financial year` DIVIDED BY `days in the part`

-- So a business started part-way through the year is a small business on its current-year test (s 6D(2)) only if that
-- annualised figure is $3,000,000 or less.
@export Is a business carried on for only part of the year small on its annualised turnover (ss 6D(2), 6DA(2))?
GIVEN `turnover earned in the part` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 6DA(1) total the business earned in the part of the year, in dollars
      `days in the part` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the part of the financial year the business was carried on
      `days in the whole financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the whole financial year (365 or 366)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a part-year business small on its annualised turnover` IF
    `What is the annual turnover for a part year` `turnover earned in the part` `days in the part` `days in the whole financial year`
        AT MOST `the small business turnover limit`

GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `its business is a small business` IF
    IF `the holder`'s `carried on the business at some time in the previous financial year`
    THEN `the holder`'s `annual turnover for the previous financial year` AT MOST `the small business turnover limit`
    ELSE `the holder`'s `annual turnover for the current year` AT MOST `the small business turnover limit`

@export Is the business that holds my information a small business operator, outside the Act (s 6D)?
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder @desc The business that holds your personal information, with its turnover figures in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the holder a small business operator` IF
        (NOT `the holder`'s `is an agency`)
    AND `its business is a small business` `the holder`
    AND (NOT (`the holder`'s `highest annual turnover for any financial year ended since it started` GREATER THAN `the small business turnover limit`))
    AND (NOT `the holder`'s `provides a health service and holds health information outside employee records`)
    AND (NOT `the holder`'s `trades in personal information without consent or legal authority`)
    AND (NOT `the holder`'s `is a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth contract`)
    AND (NOT `the holder`'s `is a credit reporting body`)
    AND (NOT `the holder`'s `is related to a body corporate whose business is not small`)

@export Is the business or agency that holds my information bound by the Australian Privacy Principles (an APP entity, s 6)?
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder @desc The business or agency that holds your personal information
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the holder bound by the APPs` IF
        `the holder`'s `is an agency`
    OR  (NOT `Is the holder a small business operator` `the holder`)
    OR  `the holder`'s `has registered a choice to be treated as an organisation`

-- s 7B(3): an act or practice of an organisation "that is or was an employer of an individual, is exempt ... if the act or
-- practice is directly related to: (a) a current or former employment relationship between the employer and the individual;
-- and (b) an employee record held by the organisation and relating to the individual."
@export Do the Australian Privacy Principles protect what my employer does with my employee record (s 7B(3))?
GIVEN `the employer` IS A Holder @desc Your employer, with its turnover figures in dollars
      `directly related to my employment and my employee record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what the employer did is directly related both to your (current or former) employment and to an employee record about you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the APPs protect my employee record` IF
        `Is the holder bound by the APPs` `the employer`
    AND (    `the employer`'s `is an agency`
         OR  (NOT `directly related to my employment and my employee record`))

§§ `Schedule 1, APP 12 -- can I see my information`

-- APP 12.1: "If an APP entity holds personal information about an individual, the entity must, on request by the individual,
-- give the individual access to the information."
-- 12.2: an agency need not, to the extent it "is required or authorised to refuse" under the Freedom of Information Act or
-- another Commonwealth access law. 12.3: an organisation need not, to the extent that one of ten grounds applies (a serious
-- threat to life, health or safety; unreasonable impact on others' privacy; frivolous or vexatious; legal proceedings
-- between us; prejudice to negotiations; unlawful; denial required by law; suspected unlawful activity; enforcement;
-- commercially sensitive evaluative information). Whether a ground applies is asked as ONE fact.
-- 12.4(a): respond "(i) if the entity is an agency--within 30 days after the request is made; or (ii) if the entity is an
-- organisation--within a reasonable period after the request is made".
-- 12.7: an agency "must not charge". 12.8: an organisation's charge "must not be excessive and must not apply to the making of
-- the request".
-- 12.9: a refusal under 12.2 or 12.3, or of the manner requested, needs "a written notice that sets out: (a) the reasons ...;
-- (b) the mechanisms available to complain about the refusal; and (c) any other matter prescribed by the regulations".
@export Must the holder give me access to the personal information it holds about me (APP 12)?
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder @desc The business or agency that holds your personal information
      `a ground to refuse applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an agency, whether a Freedom of Information ground requires or authorises refusal (APP 12.2); for an organisation, whether one of the APP 12.3 grounds applies
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the holder give me access` IF
        `Is the holder bound by the APPs` `the holder`
    AND (NOT `a ground to refuse applies`)

DECLARE `Response deadline` IS ONE OF
    `within 30 days after the request`
    `within a reasonable period after the request`
    `no deadline, because the holder is not bound by the APPs`

-- APP 12.4(a) and 13.5(a) give the same deadlines.
@export By when must the holder respond to my request to see or correct my information (APP 12.4, 13.5)?
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder @desc The business or agency that holds your personal information
GIVETH A `Response deadline`
DECIDE `By when must the holder respond to my request` IS
    IF NOT `Is the holder bound by the APPs` `the holder`
    THEN `no deadline, because the holder is not bound by the APPs`
    ELSE IF `the holder`'s `is an agency`
         THEN `within 30 days after the request`
         ELSE `within a reasonable period after the request`

DECLARE `Access charge` IS ONE OF
    `nothing`
    `a charge for giving access that is not excessive, and nothing for making the request`
    `the APPs do not limit it`

@export What may the holder charge me for access to my information (APP 12.7, 12.8)?
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder @desc The business or agency that holds your personal information
GIVETH AN `Access charge`
DECIDE `What may I be charged for access` IS
    IF NOT `Is the holder bound by the APPs` `the holder`
    THEN `the APPs do not limit it`
    ELSE IF `the holder`'s `is an agency`
         THEN `nothing`
         ELSE `a charge for giving access that is not excessive, and nothing for making the request`

@export If access is refused, must I be given written reasons and told how to complain (APP 12.9)?
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder @desc The business or agency that holds your personal information
      `refused because of a ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the holder refused access because of an APP 12.2 or 12.3 ground
      `refused the manner I asked for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the holder refused to give access in the way you asked
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I get a written notice of the refusal` IF
        `Is the holder bound by the APPs` `the holder`
    AND (`refused because of a ground` OR `refused the manner I asked for`)

§§ `Schedule 1, APP 13 -- can I have it corrected`

-- APP 13.1: if an APP entity holds personal information and "(b) either: (i) the entity is satisfied that, having regard to a
-- purpose for which the information is held, the information is inaccurate, out-of-date, incomplete, irrelevant or misleading;
-- or (ii) the individual requests the entity to correct the information; the entity must take such steps (if any) as are
-- reasonable in the circumstances to correct that information to ensure that ... the information is accurate, up-to-date,
-- complete, relevant and not misleading."
-- On a request the duty is triggered without the entity being satisfied; the steps are "(if any)", so information that is
-- already accurate needs none. The encoder's reading: a duty to take steps arises when the information is in fact
-- inaccurate, out-of-date, incomplete, irrelevant or misleading -- asked as a fact.
-- 13.3: a refusal needs a written notice with reasons and "the mechanisms available to complain". 13.4: on refusal, if the
-- individual asks, the entity "must take such steps as are reasonable in the circumstances to associate the statement".
-- 13.5(b): it "must not charge the individual for the making of the request, for correcting the personal information or for
-- associating the statement".
@export Must the holder take steps to correct my information when I ask (APP 13.1)?
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder @desc The business or agency that holds your personal information
      `I asked for a correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked the holder to correct the information
      `the holder is satisfied it is wrong` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the holder is itself satisfied the information is inaccurate, out-of-date, incomplete, irrelevant or misleading
      `it is wrong` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information is in fact inaccurate, out-of-date, incomplete, irrelevant or misleading, having regard to the purpose for which it is held
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the holder correct my information` IF
        `Is the holder bound by the APPs` `the holder`
    AND (`I asked for a correction` OR `the holder is satisfied it is wrong`)
    AND `it is wrong`

@export If the holder refuses my correction, must it attach my statement that the information is wrong (APP 13.4)?
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder @desc The business or agency that holds your personal information
      `it refused my correction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the holder refused to correct the information as you asked
      `I asked it to associate a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked it to attach a statement that the information is inaccurate, out-of-date, incomplete, irrelevant or misleading
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the holder attach my statement` IF
        `Is the holder bound by the APPs` `the holder`
    AND `it refused my correction`
    AND `I asked it to associate a statement`

@export Is it free to ask for a correction, to have it made, and to have my statement attached (APP 13.5(b))?
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder @desc The business or agency that holds your personal information
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a correction free under APP 13` IF
    `Is the holder bound by the APPs` `the holder`

§§ `Schedule 1, APP 7 -- can I stop the marketing`

-- APP 7.1: "If an organisation holds personal information about an individual, the organisation must not use or disclose
-- the information for the purpose of direct marketing."
-- 7.2: allowed for information other than sensitive information if "(a) the organisation collected the information from the
-- individual; and (b) the individual would reasonably expect" that use; "(c) the organisation provides a simple means by which
-- the individual may easily request not to receive direct marketing communications"; "(d) the individual has not made such a
-- request".
-- 7.3: allowed for other non-sensitive information (collected from someone else, or not reasonably expected) if "(b) either:
-- (i) the individual has consented ...; or (ii) it is impracticable to obtain that consent", there is a simple opt-out, "(d)
-- in each direct marketing communication" the organisation states (or draws attention to the fact) that the individual may
-- opt out, and "(e) the individual has not made such a request".
-- 7.4: sensitive information only "if the individual has consented". 7.5: contracted service providers meeting a
-- Commonwealth contract obligation.
-- 7.6, 7.7: on a request not to receive direct marketing the organisation "must not charge" and "must give effect to the
-- request within a reasonable period".
-- 7.8: "This principle does not apply to the extent that any of the following apply: ... (a) the Do Not Call Register Act
-- 2006; (b) the Spam Act 2003". Whether either applies is a question for those Acts: an INPUT here.
DECLARE `Marketing use` HAS
    `the Do Not Call Register Act or Spam Act applies to it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information is sensitive information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `collected from me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I would reasonably expect this use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I consented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consent was impracticable to obtain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a simple opt-out means is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
    `each communication says I may opt out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have asked not to receive direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to meet a Commonwealth contract obligation` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the use` IS A `Marketing use`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exception in APP 7.2 to 7.5 applies` IF
        (    (NOT `the use`'s `the information is sensitive information`)
         AND `the use`'s `collected from me`
         AND `the use`'s `I would reasonably expect this use`
         AND `the use`'s `a simple opt-out means is provided`
         AND (NOT `the use`'s `I have asked not to receive direct marketing`))
    OR  (    (NOT `the use`'s `the information is sensitive information`)
         AND ((NOT `the use`'s `collected from me`) OR (NOT `the use`'s `I would reasonably expect this use`))
         AND (`the use`'s `I consented` OR `the use`'s `consent was impracticable to obtain`)
         AND `the use`'s `a simple opt-out means is provided`
         AND `the use`'s `each communication says I may opt out`
         AND (NOT `the use`'s `I have asked not to receive direct marketing`))
    OR  (`the use`'s `the information is sensitive information` AND `the use`'s `I consented`)
    OR  `the use`'s `to meet a Commonwealth contract obligation`

DECLARE `Marketing answer` IS ONE OF
    `APP 7 does not reach it, because the marketer is not bound by the APPs`
    `APP 7 does not reach it, because the Do Not Call Register Act or the Spam Act applies`
    `APP 7 allows it`
    `APP 7 forbids it`

@export May this business use my information to send me direct marketing (APP 7)?
GIVEN `the marketer` IS A Holder @desc The business sending the marketing
      `the use` IS A `Marketing use` @desc How the business got your information and what you have said to it
GIVETH A `Marketing answer`
DECIDE `May the business market to me` IS
    IF NOT `Is the holder bound by the APPs` `the marketer`
    THEN `APP 7 does not reach it, because the marketer is not bound by the APPs`
    ELSE IF `the use`'s `the Do Not Call Register Act or Spam Act applies to it`
         THEN `APP 7 does not reach it, because the Do Not Call Register Act or the Spam Act applies`
         ELSE IF `an exception in APP 7.2 to 7.5 applies` `the use`
              THEN `APP 7 allows it`
              ELSE `APP 7 forbids it`

@export If I ask the business to stop direct marketing, must it stop within a reasonable period and free of charge (APP 7.7)?
GIVEN `the marketer` IS A Holder @desc The business sending the marketing
      `the use` IS A `Marketing use` @desc How the business got your information and what you have said to it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the business stop when I ask` IF
        `Is the holder bound by the APPs` `the marketer`
    AND (NOT `the use`'s `the Do Not Call Register Act or Spam Act applies to it`)

§§ `ss 6N, 21C, 21P -- what goes on my credit file, and what the lender must tell me`

-- s 6N: "Credit information about an individual is personal information (other than sensitive information) that is: (a)
-- identification information ...; (b) consumer credit liability information ...; (c) repayment history information ...; (ca)
-- financial hardship information ...; (d) a statement that an information request has been made ...; (e) the type of consumer
-- credit or commercial credit, and the amount of credit, sought in an application ...; (f) default information ...; (g)
-- payment information ...; (h) new arrangement information ...; (i) court proceedings information ...; (j) personal insolvency
-- information ...; (k) publicly available information" about activities in Australia and credit worthiness; "(l) the opinion
-- of a credit provider that the individual has committed ... a serious credit infringement".
-- Income, savings and employment are not on the list (the encoder's example of something that is not).
DECLARE `Kind of information` IS ONE OF
    `identification information`
    `consumer credit liability information`
    `repayment history information`
    `financial hardship information`
    `a statement that an information request was made`
    `the type and amount of credit sought in an application`
    `default information`
    `payment information`
    `new arrangement information`
    `court proceedings information`
    `personal insolvency information`
    `publicly available credit-worthiness information`
    `a serious credit infringement opinion`
    `sensitive information`
    `information about income or savings`

@export Is this kind of information credit information that may be on my credit file (s 6N)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of information` @desc The kind of information about you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it credit information` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `sensitive information` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `information about income or savings` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 21C(1): "At or before the time a credit provider collects personal information about an individual that the provider is
-- likely to disclose to a credit reporting body, the provider must: (a) notify the individual of ... (i) the name and contact
-- details of the body; (ii) any other matter specified in the registered CR code; or (b) otherwise ensure that the individual
-- is aware of those matters."
@export Must the lender tell me, when it collects my information, which credit reporting body it may send it to (s 21C)?
GIVEN `likely to disclose it to a credit reporting body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the credit provider is likely to pass the information it collects to a credit reporting body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the lender name the credit reporting body` IF
    `likely to disclose it to a credit reporting body`

-- s 21P(1): applies if "(a) a credit provider refuses an application for consumer credit made in Australia" by the individual,
-- "(b) the refusal is based wholly or partly on credit eligibility information" about the individual (or a guarantor or
-- co-applicant), and "(c) a credit reporting body disclosed the relevant credit reporting information to the provider for the
-- purposes of assessing the application". (2): "within a reasonable period after refusing the application", a written
-- notice that it was refused, that the refusal is based on credit eligibility information, and, if about the individual, the
-- name and contact details of the credit reporting body.
@export If my credit application is refused because of my credit report, must the lender tell me in writing and name the credit reporting body (s 21P)?
GIVEN `refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender refused your application for consumer credit made in Australia
      `based on credit eligibility information about me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the refusal was based wholly or partly on credit eligibility information about you
      `a credit reporting body disclosed it for the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a credit reporting body supplied the information to the lender to assess this application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the lender give me a refusal notice naming the bureau` IF
    `refused` AND `based on credit eligibility information about me` AND `a credit reporting body disclosed it for the application`

§§ `ss 6Q, 21D -- can my default be listed`

-- s 6Q(1): default information is information about a payment the individual is overdue in making on consumer credit if
-- "(a) the individual is at least 60 days overdue in making the payment; and (b) the provider has given a written notice to
-- the individual informing the individual of the overdue payment and requesting that the individual pay ...; and (c) the
-- provider is not prevented by a statute of limitations from recovering the amount ...; and (d) the amount of the overdue
-- payment is equal to or more than: (i) $150; or (ii) such higher amount as is prescribed by the regulations."
-- The Privacy Regulation 2013 is not deposited: the prescribed amount is an INPUT (0 if none).
-- s 21D(3): disclosure to a credit reporting body only if "(a) the information does not relate to an act, omission, matter
-- or thing that occurred or existed before the individual turned 18"; "(b) ... the credit is or has been provided, or applied
-- for, in Australia"; and for default information "(d)(i) the credit provider has given the individual a notice in writing
-- stating that the provider intends to disclose the information ...; and (ii) at least 14 days have passed since the giving
-- of the notice." (2)(a): the provider must be in a recognised external dispute resolution scheme and believe the individual
-- is at least 18; the body must have an Australian link -- asked as one fact about the provider.
DECLARE `Overdue payment` HAS
    `days overdue` IS A NUMBER
    `written notice requesting payment given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `recovery barred by a statute of limitations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount overdue` IS A NUMBER
    `higher amount prescribed by the regulations` IS A NUMBER
    `it relates to something before I turned 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the credit was provided or applied for in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provider meets the s 21D(2) conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice of intention to list given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days since that notice` IS A NUMBER

`the default floor in the Act` MEANS 150

@export Is my overdue payment default information (s 6Q)?
GIVEN `the payment` IS AN `Overdue payment` @desc The overdue payment, with days, dollar amounts and notices
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my overdue payment default information` IF
        `the payment`'s `days overdue` AT LEAST 60
    AND `the payment`'s `written notice requesting payment given`
    AND (NOT `the payment`'s `recovery barred by a statute of limitations`)
    AND `the payment`'s `amount overdue` AT LEAST `the larger of` `the default floor in the Act` (`the payment`'s `higher amount prescribed by the regulations`)

@export May the lender list my overdue payment as a default with a credit reporting body (ss 6Q, 21D)?
GIVEN `the payment` IS AN `Overdue payment` @desc The overdue payment, with days, dollar amounts and notices
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my default be listed` IF
        `Is my overdue payment default information` `the payment`
    AND `the payment`'s `the provider meets the s 21D(2) conditions`
    AND (NOT `the payment`'s `it relates to something before I turned 18`)
    AND `the payment`'s `the credit was provided or applied for in Australia`
    AND `the payment`'s `notice of intention to list given`
    AND `the payment`'s `days since that notice` AT LEAST 14

§§ `ss 20V, 20W, 20X -- how long it stays on my credit file`

-- s 20W table: consumer credit liability information, 2 years from termination; repayment history information, 2 years from
-- the due day; financial hardship information, 1 year from the due day; 6N(d) or (e) information, 5 years from the information
-- request; default information, "5 years that starts on the day on which the credit reporting body collects the information";
-- payment information, 5 years from collection of the default information; new arrangement information, 2 years; court
-- proceedings information, 5 years from the judgement; a serious credit infringement opinion, 7 years from collection.
-- s 20V(1) note: "There is no retention period for identification information or credit information of a kind referred to in
-- paragraph 6N(k)." Personal insolvency information has its own section, 20X.
-- s 20V(2): the body "must destroy the credit information, or ensure that the information is de-identified, within 1 month
-- after the retention period for the information ends".
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of information`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 20W retention period in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `consumer credit liability information` THEN 2
    WHEN `repayment history information` THEN 2
    WHEN `financial hardship information` THEN 1
    WHEN `a statement that an information request was made` THEN 5
    WHEN `the type and amount of credit sought in an application` THEN 5
    WHEN `default information` THEN 5
    WHEN `payment information` THEN 5
    WHEN `new arrangement information` THEN 2
    WHEN `court proceedings information` THEN 5
    WHEN `a serious credit infringement opinion` THEN 7
    OTHERWISE 0

@export For how many years may this kind of information stay on my credit file under s 20W (0 means s 20W sets no period)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of information` @desc The kind of credit information
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many years may it stay on my credit file` IS `the s 20W retention period in years` `the kind`

@export Has the s 20W retention period for this information on my credit file ended by this day?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of information` @desc The kind of credit information
      `the period starts on` IS A NUMBER @desc The day the s 20W period starts (for a default, the day the bureau collected it), as YYYYMMDD
      `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you are asking about, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the retention period ended` IF
        `the s 20W retention period in years` `the kind` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the day` AT LEAST `the anniversary` `the period starts on` (`the s 20W retention period in years` `the kind`)

-- s 20X(1) table, retention period "whichever of the following periods ends later": item 4, "a debt agreement to which item 5
-- of this table does not apply": "(a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is made; (b) the
-- period of 2 years that starts on the day: (i) the agreement is terminated under the Bankruptcy Act; or (ii) an order
-- declaring that all the agreement is void is made". Item 5, "a debt agreement that ends under section 185N of the
-- Bankruptcy Act": "(a) the period of 5 years that starts on the day on which the agreement is made; (b) the period that ends
-- on the day on which the agreement ends."
DECLARE `How the agreement ended` IS ONE OF
    `ended under s 185N`
    `terminated or declared void`
    `not yet ended`

DECLARE `Debt agreement` HAS
    `made on` IS A NUMBER
    `how it ended` IS A `How the agreement ended`
    `ended on` IS A NUMBER

@export Has the retention period for my debt agreement on my credit file ended by this day (s 20X items 4 and 5)?
GIVEN `the agreement` IS A `Debt agreement` @desc Your debt agreement under Part IX of the Bankruptcy Act: the day it was made and how and when it ended, as YYYYMMDD
      `the day` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you are asking about, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my debt agreement retention period ended` IF
        `the day` AT LEAST `the anniversary` (`the agreement`'s `made on`) 5
    AND (CONSIDER `the agreement`'s `how it ended`
         WHEN `ended under s 185N` THEN `the day` GREATER THAN `the agreement`'s `ended on`
         WHEN `terminated or declared void` THEN `the day` AT LEAST `the anniversary` (`the agreement`'s `ended on`) 2
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

`the months after the retention period within which it must be destroyed or de-identified` MEANS 1

§§ `ss 20K, 20R, 20T -- my rights against the credit reporting body`

-- s 20R(1): "If a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information about an individual, the body must, on request by
-- an access seeker ..., give the access seeker access". (2): except to the extent that giving access would be unlawful,
-- denial is required by law or a court order, or access would prejudice enforcement -- one fact.
-- (3): "within a reasonable period, but not longer than 10 days, after the request is made".
-- (5): "If a request ... has not been made to the credit reporting body in the previous 3 months, the body must not charge".
-- (6): otherwise any charge "must not be excessive and must not apply to the making of the request".
@export Must the credit reporting body give me my credit report (s 20R)?
GIVEN `an exception in s 20R(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether giving access would be unlawful, denial is required by law or a court or tribunal order, or access would prejudice enforcement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the bureau give me my credit report` IF
    NOT `an exception in s 20R(2) applies`

@export What is the most days the credit reporting body may take to respond to my request for my credit report (s 20R(3))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days may the bureau take to give me my report` IS 10

@export Is my credit report free (s 20R(5))?
GIVEN `I asked this body in the previous 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made an access request to this same credit reporting body in the 3 months before this request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my credit report free` IF
    NOT `I asked this body in the previous 3 months`

-- s 20T(2): if the body "is satisfied that the personal information is inaccurate, out-of-date, incomplete, irrelevant or
-- misleading", it must take reasonable steps to correct it "within: (a) the period of 30 days that starts on the day on which
-- the request is made; or (b) such longer period as the individual has agreed to in writing". (5): "must not charge".
-- s 20U(3): if not corrected, a written notice with reasons, evidence, and that the individual may go to a recognised external
-- dispute resolution scheme or complain to the Commissioner.
@export Within how many days must the credit reporting body correct my credit file (s 20T(2))?
GIVEN `the bureau is satisfied it is wrong` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the credit reporting body is satisfied the information is inaccurate, out-of-date, incomplete, irrelevant or misleading
      `longer period I agreed in writing` IS A NUMBER @desc A longer period in days you agreed to in writing, or 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must my credit file be corrected` IS
    IF `the bureau is satisfied it is wrong`
    THEN `the larger of` 30 `longer period I agreed in writing`
    ELSE 0

-- s 20K(1): if "(b) the individual believes on reasonable grounds that the individual has been, or is likely to be, a victim
-- of fraud (including identity fraud); and (c) the individual requests the body not to use or disclose the information", the
-- body "must not use or disclose the information during the ban period", unless (2) the individual consents in writing or the
-- law requires. (3): the ban period ends "21 days after the day on which the request is made" unless extended under (4).
-- (6): no charge.
@export If I fear identity fraud, must the credit reporting body freeze my credit file (s 20K)?
GIVEN `I believe on reasonable grounds I am or may be a fraud victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you believe on reasonable grounds you have been, or are likely to be, a victim of fraud, including identity fraud
      `I asked the body not to use or disclose it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked the credit reporting body not to use or disclose your credit reporting information
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the bureau freeze my file` IF
    `I believe on reasonable grounds I am or may be a fraud victim` AND `I asked the body not to use or disclose it`

`the days a ban period lasts unless extended` MEANS 21

§§ `Part IIIC, ss 26WE, 26WF, 26WG -- was there an eligible data breach`

-- s 26WE(1)(a): the Part applies where "an APP entity holds personal information" and is bound by APP 11.1. (2): an eligible
-- data breach is "(a) ... unauthorised access to, or unauthorised disclosure of, the information" where "(ii) a reasonable
-- person would conclude that the access or disclosure would be likely to result in serious harm to any of the individuals to
-- whom the information relates"; or "(b) the information is lost in circumstances where: (i) unauthorised access to, or
-- unauthorised disclosure of, the information is likely to occur" and serious harm would be likely if it did. "(d) an
-- individual covered by subparagraph (a)(ii) or (b)(ii) is at risk from the eligible data breach."
-- s 26WF(1), (3): it "is not, and is taken never to have been" an eligible data breach if the entity's action, before serious
-- harm (or, for a loss, before access), means a reasonable person would conclude serious harm is not likely. (2): if that is
-- so for a particular individual only, the Part does not require that individual to be notified.
-- s 26WG lists matters for "serious harm" (kind and sensitivity of the information, security, who has it, "any other relevant
-- matters"). It does not say whether a given kind of information qualifies: an INPUT.
DECLARE `Kind of incident` IS ONE OF
    `unauthorised access or disclosure`
    `loss of the information`

DECLARE `Data incident` HAS
    `what happened` IS A `Kind of incident`
    `after the loss, unauthorised access or disclosure is likely` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reasonable person would conclude serious harm is likely` IS A BOOLEAN
    `remedial action took it out for everyone` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is what happened to my information an eligible data breach (s 26WE)?
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder @desc The business or agency that held your information
      `the incident` IS A `Data incident` @desc What happened to the information
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it an eligible data breach` IF
        `Is the holder bound by the APPs` `the holder`
    AND `the incident`'s `a reasonable person would conclude serious harm is likely`
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `remedial action took it out for everyone`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the incident`'s `what happened`
         WHEN `unauthorised access or disclosure` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE `the incident`'s `after the loss, unauthorised access or disclosure is likely`)

§§ `Part IIIC, ss 26WH, 26WK, 26WL -- must I be told`

-- s 26WH: where the entity "is aware that there are reasonable grounds to suspect" an eligible data breach but not that there
-- are reasonable grounds to believe one, it must "carry out a reasonable and expeditious assessment" and "take all reasonable
-- steps to ensure that the assessment is completed within 30 days after the entity becomes aware".
-- s 26WK(2): once aware of reasonable grounds to believe, "prepare a statement" and "give a copy of the statement to the
-- Commissioner", "as soon as practicable after the entity becomes so aware". (3): identity and contact details, a
-- description, the kinds of information, and "recommendations about the steps that individuals should take".
-- s 26WL(2): "(a) if it is practicable ... to notify the contents of the statement to each of the individuals to whom the
-- relevant information relates--take such steps as are reasonable ... to notify ... each of" them; "or (b) if it is
-- practicable ... to each of the individuals who are at risk from the eligible data breach" -- those; "or (c) if neither
-- paragraph (a) nor (b) applies: (i) publish a copy of the statement on the entity's website (if any); and (ii) take
-- reasonable steps to publicise" it. (3): "as soon as practicable after the completion of the preparation of the statement."
-- The encoder's reading of "or": where both (a) and (b) are practicable the entity may take either, so an individual who is at
-- risk is told directly either way, and one who is not at risk is told only if the entity takes (a).
-- No section fixes a number of days for the statement or the notification. The 30 days is for ASSESSING a suspicion.
`the days within which reasonable steps must complete an assessment` MEANS 30

DECLARE `Breach notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `I need not be told, because it is not an eligible data breach`
    `not yet: the holder must first assess its suspicion, taking reasonable steps to finish within 30 days`
    `I must be told directly, as soon as practicable after the statement to the Commissioner is prepared`
    `I may be told directly, but need not be, because I am not at risk`
    `I need not be told, because remedial action means serious harm to me is not likely`
    `I need not be told directly, because I am not at risk and only those at risk will be told`
    `the statement must be published on the holder's website and publicised`

@export Must I be told about a data breach of my information, and how (ss 26WH, 26WK, 26WL)?
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder @desc The business or agency that held your information
      `the incident` IS A `Data incident` @desc What happened to the information
      `the holder has grounds to believe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the holder is aware there are reasonable grounds to believe there has been an eligible data breach (not merely to suspect one)
      `I am at risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person would conclude the breach is likely to result in serious harm to you
      `remedial action protects me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the holder acted before harm so that serious harm to you is no longer likely (s 26WF(2))
      `practicable to notify everyone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is practicable to notify everyone whose information was involved
      `practicable to notify those at risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is practicable to notify everyone at risk
GIVETH A `Breach notice answer`
DECIDE `Must I be told of the breach` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Is it an eligible data breach` `the holder` `the incident`
            THEN `I need not be told, because it is not an eligible data breach`
        IF NOT `the holder has grounds to believe`
            THEN `not yet: the holder must first assess its suspicion, taking reasonable steps to finish within 30 days`
        IF `remedial action protects me`
            THEN `I need not be told, because remedial action means serious harm to me is not likely`
        IF (NOT `practicable to notify everyone`) AND (NOT `practicable to notify those at risk`)
            THEN `the statement must be published on the holder's website and publicised`
        IF `I am at risk`
            THEN `I must be told directly, as soon as practicable after the statement to the Commissioner is prepared`
        IF `practicable to notify everyone`
            THEN `I may be told directly, but need not be, because I am not at risk`
        OTHERWISE `I need not be told directly, because I am not at risk and only those at risk will be told`

@export Must the holder send a statement about the breach to the Commissioner (s 26WK)?
GIVEN `the holder` IS A Holder @desc The business or agency that held your information
      `the incident` IS A `Data incident` @desc What happened to the information
      `the holder has grounds to believe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the holder is aware there are reasonable grounds to believe there has been an eligible data breach
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commissioner be given a statement` IF
    `Is it an eligible data breach` `the holder` `the incident` AND `the holder has grounds to believe`

§§ `Part V, ss 36, 40, 41 -- will the Commissioner take my complaint`

-- s 36(1): "An individual may complain to the Commissioner about an act or practice that may be an interference with the
-- privacy of the individual." (3): "A complaint shall be in writing." (5): "The complaint shall specify the respondent".
-- s 40(1): the Commissioner "shall investigate" (subject to (1A) and s 41). (1A): "The Commissioner must not investigate a
-- complaint if the complainant did not complain to the respondent before making the complaint to the Commissioner ...
-- However, the Commissioner may decide to investigate the complaint if he or she considers that it was not appropriate for the
-- complainant to complain to the respondent." (1B): (1A) "does not apply if the complaint is about an act or practice that may
-- breach: (a) section 20R, 20T, 21T or 21V (which are about access to, and correction of, credit reporting information etc.)".
-- s 41(1)(c): the Commissioner "may decide not to investigate" if satisfied that "the complaint was made more than 12 months
-- after the complainant became aware of the act or practice". The other s 41 grounds are not encoded.
DECLARE Complaint HAS
    `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `names the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I complained to the respondent first` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner considers complaining first was not appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `about access to or correction of credit reporting information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day I became aware` IS A NUMBER
    `the day I complain` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Complaint answer` IS ONE OF
    `not yet a complaint: it must be in writing and name the respondent`
    `the Commissioner must not investigate until I have complained to the respondent`
    `the Commissioner must investigate, but may decline because I complained more than 12 months after I became aware`
    `the Commissioner must investigate, subject to the other grounds in s 41`

@export Will the Information Commissioner investigate my privacy complaint (ss 36, 40, 41(1)(c))?
GIVEN `the complaint` IS A Complaint @desc Your complaint, with the day you became aware of the act and the day you complain, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A `Complaint answer`
DECIDE `Will my complaint be investigated` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the complaint`'s `in writing`) OR (NOT `the complaint`'s `names the respondent`)
            THEN `not yet a complaint: it must be in writing and name the respondent`
        IF     (NOT `the complaint`'s `I complained to the respondent first`)
           AND (NOT `the complaint`'s `about access to or correction of credit reporting information`)
           AND (NOT `the complaint`'s `the Commissioner considers complaining first was not appropriate`)
            THEN `the Commissioner must not investigate until I have complained to the respondent`
        IF `the complaint`'s `the day I complain` GREATER THAN `the anniversary` (`the complaint`'s `the day I became aware`) 1
            THEN `the Commissioner must investigate, but may decline because I complained more than 12 months after I became aware`
        OTHERWISE `the Commissioner must investigate, subject to the other grounds in s 41`
